                <pb facs="0514" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1946v02/pg492"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865C.01/6–1346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Secretary of State, at
                        Paris</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-13">June 13, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2833. Secdel 259. For the Secretary. Following
                    telegram addressed to you has been received from Abdelrahman Azzam Secy Gen
                    League Arab States: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Report was brought to notice Council League Arab States meeting now
                            Bloudan Syria that British Govt proposed to Council Foreign Ministers
                            that delegation be sent Tripolitania Cyrenaica to investigate wishes and
                            desires of people concerning their political future. Arab League Council
                            unanimously authorised me convey Your Excellency and other Foreign
                            Ministers that they are directly concerned with future of these Arabs
                            and that under pact of Arab League they must support with all means
                            development of rights and interests of Arabs Lybia. Therefore League is
                            anxious to be represented in any delegation for investigations in Lybia.
                            In case British proposal accepted we are anxious to be invited to take
                            part and be given notice of time and procedures. With best wishes and
                            highest consideration.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
